    {
      "abbreviated": false,
      "abstract": "A Lean 4 / Mathlib formalization of two basic results of spectral graph theory, stated through the adjacency quadratic form on vectors orthogonal to the all-ones vector: the expander mixing lemma of Alon and Chung (for a d-regular graph on n \u2265 2 vertices with |x\u00b7Ax| \u2264 \u03bc\u2016x\u2016\u00b2 on \ud835\udfd9\u22a5, |e(S,T) \u2212 d|S||T|/n| \u2264 \u03bc\u221a(|S||T|)), and the Alon\u2013Boppana bound in Nilli's form (a d-regular graph, d \u2265 2, with two vertices at distance at least 2k + 4 has a nonzero x \u27c2 \ud835\udfd9 with x\u00b7Ax \u2265 (2\u221a(d\u22121) \u2212 (2\u221a(d\u22121) \u2212 1)/(k+1))\u2016x\u2016\u00b2). Mathlib has adjacency matrices but neither result.",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "Juan Pablo Traverso Gianini"
        }
      ],
      "classification": {
        "arxiv": [
          "math.CO"
        ],
        "msc2020": [
          "05C50",
          "05C48"
        ]
      },
      "formalization": {
        "theorem_names": [
          "ExpanderTheorem.expander_mixing",
          "ExpanderTheorem.alon_boppana"
        ]
      },
